  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving food security of crises affected households through increased staple food production.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed project aims to improve food security among 2,500 vulnerable households by increasing the production of staple food in Habila County. Over a 10-month implementation period, the project will provide targeted households with seeds, training, farm labour and support to adopt sustainable and climate-resilient farming practices. The initiative will improve household food availability, and resilience against food shortages. The project participants will be provided with 10kgs of sorghum, 5 kgs of legume crop and 1 kg of oil seed type. The farm labour support will aim to support each project benefiting HH with tractor ploughing services covering at least 1 hectare (2.25 Feddans) of farmland. The target beneficiaries will receive trainings (in integrated Pest management, production and use of organic fertilizers, post-harvest processing, seeds conservation and seed generation. The project beneficiaries will be organized in farmer field schools, where they will be trained and encouraged to learn from each other.&#xa0; ltbrgtThe target group will be selected based on wide consultation with stakeholders during project inception. Priority will be giving to HHs with land access who did not farm during the immediate past rainy season because of lack of seeds, tools and farm labour. The proposed project will be implemented in partnership with KODI, a national NGO with local community acceptance and experience in implementing similar project in the area.&#xa0; ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
